## 4. Clinical Safety Design

### 4.1 Human-in-the-Loop Requirement

**No automated action permitted at any risk tier.** All outputs are decision-support tools. This is non-negotiable:

1. NLP models have error rates — human judgment corrects them
2. Models cannot know about bereavement, family crisis, or illness
3. The counsellor reaching out IS the therapeutic intervention

### 4.2 False Negative Priority

In mental health screening, **missed cases are more harmful than false alarms.** The pipeline is tuned to:

- Accept higher false positive rates at Tier 1
- Use Tier 2 to reduce false positives before escalation
- Reserve human review for all high-risk Tier 3 outputs

### 4.3 Minimum Viable Safety Standards

Before any pilot deployment:

- [ ] IRB/ethics board approval
- [ ] Informed consent protocol (adolescents + parents/guardians)
- [ ] Counsellor training on pipeline outputs
- [ ] Clear escalation pathways to REACH, IMH, and emergency services
- [ ] Incident review process for missed crises
- [ ] Quarterly model revalidation against clinical outcomes
- [ ] PDPA compliance review

