## 5. Limitations and Honest Assessment

### 5.1 What This Pipeline Cannot Do

- **Diagnose** mental health conditions — screening tool only
- **Replace** clinical assessment — triages, not diagnoses
- **Guarantee** detection — no screening tool achieves 100% sensitivity
- **Account** for all cultural nuances — Indian and Malay communities underrepresented

### 5.2 Known Biases

| Bias | Description | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| Training data origin | Weibo (China) — may not represent Singapore | Singapore validation in Phase 2 |
| Language coverage | Optimised for Simplified Chinese | T→S conversion + bilingual validation |
| Platform bias | Social media only | Complementary self-report integration |
| Demographic gaps | Limited Malay/Indian validation | Stratified validation by ethnicity |
| Temporal drift | Language evolves | Quarterly revalidation |

### 5.3 What Success Looks Like

A successfully deployed pipeline would:
- Identify at-risk adolescents 2–4 weeks earlier than current referral pathways
- Reduce counsellor time spent on reactive crisis management
- Increase proportion receiving proactive outreach
- Generate longitudinal data on Singapore adolescent mental health trajectories

